import mundane definition stdlib/divisibility/even
import mundane theorem    stdlib/divisibility/even-or-odd
import mundane theorem    stdlib/divisibility/not-both
import mundane definition stdlib/divisibility/odd

theorem cubic-sum-even-iff-even
  note        An integer is even or odd. If a = 2k, then a³ + a² + a is
              8k³ + 4k² + 2k, twice 4k³ + 2k² + k. If a = 2k + 1, it is
              8k³ + 16k² + 12k + 3, twice 4k³ + 8k² + 6k + 1, plus 1, which
              is odd and so not even.
  let a ∈ ℤ                                                           (H1)
  then a³ + a² + a is even ↔ a is even

1.  a³ + a² + a is even ↔ a is even
    both directions

    direction
    assume a³ + a² + a is even                                        (D1)

    1.1.  a is even or a is odd
          mun:even-or-odd n := a

    1.2.  a is even
          cases, from 1.1

          case
          assume a is even, which is the claim                        (C1)

          case
          assume a is odd                                             (C2)

          1.2.1.  k ∈ ℤ. a = 2k + 1.
                  obtain k: mun:odd, from C2

          1.2.2.  a³ + a² + a = 2(4k³ + 8k² + 6k + 1) + 1
                  algebra, from 1.2.1

          1.2.3.  a³ + a² + a is odd
                  mun:odd n := a³ + a² + a, from 1.2.2

          1.2.4.  a³ + a² + a is not odd
                  mun:not-both n := a³ + a² + a, from D1, contradicting 1.2.3

    direction
    assume a is even                                                  (D2)

    1.3.  k ∈ ℤ. a = 2k.
          obtain k: mun:even, from D2

    1.4.  a³ + a² + a = 2(4k³ + 2k² + k)
          algebra, from 1.3

    1.5.  a³ + a² + a is even
          mun:even n := a³ + a² + a, from 1.4
